{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.root_angle_ratio_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.root_angle_ratio_A2","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L160-L170","doc":"The root angle `cos θ = a₁₂/a₁₁ = -1/2`, hence `θ = 120°`.\nBoth entries are fixed integers, so the ratio is q-independent.\n\n§7c: stated **division-free over the Cartan datum's own ring ℤ**, as the\ncross-multiplied identity `2·a₁₂ = -a₁₁`.  This is the R[h] pattern — the\nratio claim `a₁₂/a₁₁ = -1/2` is recovered from it in any ℚ-algebra by\ndividing through by the unit `a₁₁ = 2`, so nothing is lost by not passing\nto ℚ, and the integrality of the Cartan entries stays visible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_eq_cartan_at_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_eq_cartan_at_classical","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L152-L156","doc":"At q = 1, the coincidence: [2]₁ = 2·1 = 2 = a₁₁.\nThis numerical accident is the source of the confusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartan_fixed_while_qSerre_moves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartan_fixed_while_qSerre_moves","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L144-L150","doc":"**The \"two 2s\" separation.**  The Cartan datum is constant in `q` while the\nSerre coefficient is not: they cannot be the same object.  This conjunction —\nnot either half alone — is the file's actual claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:q-deformation-weight-lattice","label":"rem:q-deformation-weight-lattice","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/q-deformation-weight-lattice.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_not_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_not_constant","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L133-L142","doc":"The Serre coefficient genuinely **moves** with `q`: it is not a constant\nfunction, witnessed at `q = 2` where the framed binomial is `5` and the framed\nCartan diagonal is `4`.\n\nThis is the half of the \"two 2s\" separation that has content — without it,\n`cartanMatrixAt_const` is compatible with both sides being constant, which is\nprecisely the confusion the file exists to dispel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_neq_cartan_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.qSerre_neq_cartan_diag","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L116-L131","doc":"For `q ≠ 1` — stated as `(q - 1)² ≠ 0`, the honest upstream hypothesis —\nthe framed Gaussian binomial differs from the framed Cartan diagonal.  The\nCartan entry stays `2`; the Serre coefficient moves.  They are different\nmathematical objects.\n\nThe hypothesis is genuinely upstream of the conclusion: the proof supplies the\nidentity `(q² + 1) - 2q = (q - 1)²`.  (An earlier version took `q² + 1 ≠ 2q`\nas the hypothesis, which is definitionally the conclusion — it assumed what it\nclaimed to prove.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.serre_exponent_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.serre_exponent_A2","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L110-L112","doc":"Serre exponent: 1 - a₁₂ = 2.  The binomial C(2,1) = 2 that gets\nq-deformed to [2]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartan_A2_offdiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartan_A2_offdiag","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L107-L108","doc":"Off-diagonal entry: a₁₂ = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrixAt_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrixAt_const","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L93-L105","doc":"The A₂ Cartan datum is constant in `q`.\n\n**This is true by construction, not a discovery** — `cartanMatrixAt` ignores its\nargument, so the statement is `rfl`, and it carries no information on its own.\nIt is recorded only as the trivial half of the \"two 2s\" separation; the half\nwith content is `qSerre_not_constant` below, and the separation itself is\n`cartan_fixed_while_qSerre_moves`.\n\nDo **not** cite this lemma as evidence that the substrate's `q₀` cannot reach\nthe root datum: that is a theorem of Drinfeld–Jimbo quantisation\n(Lusztig/Kashiwara), which this file does not formalise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrixAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrixAt","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The Cartan datum the quantisation functor consumes, presented as a\n`q`-indexed family so that \"does not depend on `q`\" is a statement one\ncan actually write down.  The parameter is deliberately ignored. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrix_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.cartanMatrix_A2","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L83-L85","doc":"The A₂ Cartan matrix: `[[2, -1], [-1, 2]]`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:a2-from-three-strands","label":"prop:a2-from-three-strands","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/a2-from-three-strands.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.gaussianBinomial2_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.gaussianBinomial2_classical","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L76-L79","doc":"At q = 1, the framed Gaussian binomial is 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.gaussianBinomial2Framed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.WeylInvarianceQDeformation.gaussianBinomial2Framed","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/WeylInvarianceQDeformation.lean#L70-L74","doc":"The framed Gaussian binomial: q · [2]_q = q² + 1.\nWorking in framed form so the file lives over a generic `CommRing`\nwith no inverses and no archimedean input (§7c wall discipline). ","signatureChunk":0}]}